{"timestamp":"2026-04-24T08:19:09.989Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"We know from the raw Codex rollout records.\n\nLocal Codex is `codex-cli 0.124.0`, and its transcript `token_count` events include both aggregate and subset fields. In multiple real records, the invariant is:\n\n```text\ntotal_tokens == input_tokens + output_tokens\n```\n\nnot:\n\n```text\ninput_tokens + cached_input_tokens + output_tokens + reasoning_output_tokens\n```\n\nConcrete example from a local Codex transcript we inspected:\n\n```text\ninput_tokens: 123302\ncached_input_tokens: 96128\noutput_tokens: 1944\nreasoning_output_tokens: 1129\ntotal_tokens: 125246\n```\n\nThe math:\n\n```text\n123302 + 1944 = 125246\n```\n\nSo `cached_input_tokens` is inside `input_tokens`, and `reasoning_output_tokens` is inside `output_tokens`. If they were additive, Codex’s own `total_tokens` would be much larger.\n\nSame pattern appears in `last_token_usage` too, for example:\n\n```text\ninput_tokens: 33798\ncached_input_tokens: 32768\noutput_tokens: 413\nreasoning_output_tokens: 232\ntotal_tokens: 34211\n\n33798 + 413 = 34211\n```\n\nThat is why the fix normalizes Codex’s inclusive fields into Entire’s additive model. Since Entire totals by summing its fields, we need to split cached input out of input, and avoid adding reasoning output again.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
