{"timestamp":"2026-04-24T08:20:22.319Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Because `TokenUsage` is agent-agnostic and component-based. It stores:\n\n```text\nInputTokens\nCacheCreationTokens\nCacheReadTokens\nOutputTokens\nSubagentTokens\n```\n\nThere is no `TotalTokens` field in the shared model. Status/explain/checkpoint display calculates total by summing those fields so it works across Claude, Codex, Gemini, Droid, Copilot, and subagents.\n\nFor Codex specifically, we could use `total_tokens` as a validation source, but not as the only stored value, because we still want the breakdown:\n\n```text\nfresh input vs cached input vs output\n```\n\nAlso, Codex’s `total_tokens` is cumulative in the transcript, so for checkpoint-scoped metadata we would still need to subtract the baseline total from the latest total.\n\nThe practical rule is:\n\n```text\nCodex total_tokens_delta should equal Entire normalized field sum\n```\n\nSo `total_tokens` is useful as an invariant/test oracle. The bug was that our Codex fields were not normalized into Entire’s additive representation before the shared summing code saw them.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
